Topics Covered:
1.  Transport Layer Overview
2.  Process-to-Process Communication
3.  TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)
4.  UDP (User Datagram Protocol)
5.  TCP vs UDP
6.  TCP 3-Way Handshake
7.  TCP Reliability
8.  Sequence Numbers
9.  Acknowledgment Numbers
10. Retransmission
11. Checksum
12. Flow Control
13. Receive Window (rwnd)
14. Sliding Window
15. Congestion Control
16. Congestion Window (cwnd)
17. Slow Start
18. Congestion Avoidance
19. Duplicate ACKs
20. Fast Retransmit
21. Port Numbers
22. Socket Basics

Key Takeaways:
- Understood process-to-process communication at the Transport Layer.
- Learned the differences between TCP and UDP.
- Understood TCP connection establishment using:
  SYN → SYN-ACK → ACK.
- Learned how TCP provides reliable and ordered delivery.
- Understood sequence numbers, acknowledgments, checksum, and retransmission.
- Learned flow control and the role of the receive window (rwnd).
- Understood congestion control and the congestion window (cwnd).
- Learned the basic concepts of Slow Start and Congestion Avoidance.
- Understood the difference between flow control and congestion control.
- Learned that IP identifies a host while a port identifies a process/application.
- Learned important port numbers such as HTTP (80), HTTPS (443), SSH (22), DNS (53), and FTP (21).
- Understood the basic concept of a network socket.
